<title>USA: Johnstown America Q3 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Johnstown America Q3 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	  loss	  $0.16   profit	 $0.03</p>
<p> Net	  loss	  1,563   profit	   261</p>
<p> Revs		     140,845		  166,881</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   9,741		    9,808</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q3 1996 non cash amortization, net of tax, $2.1 million or $0.21/share, vs $1.2 million or $0.12 a year ago.  </p>
<p>Full name is Johnstown America Industries Inc</p>
<p>		     NINE MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	 loss	   $0.36   profit	 $1.10</p>
<p> Net	 loss	   3,515   profit	10,822</p>
<p> Revs		     426,474		  512,049</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   9,757		    9,810</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Nine-month 1996 results include non-cash amortization net of tax of $6.2 million or $0.63/share vs $2.7 million or $0.28 a year ago.</p>
<p>Nine-month 1995 results pro forma as if Bostrom Seating Inc and Truck Components Inc acquisitions had taken place on January 1, 1995. Excluding pro forma adjustments, nine-month 1995 net income was $6,576,000 or $0.67 a share.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
